{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"f14207a6-887b-4c18-a340-f541176ea4a0","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Why Session Replay Was Empty on the New UI\n\nIn Flutter, PostHog session replay works by capturing screenshots of the widget tree using `PostHogWidget`. Without `PostHogWidget` wrapping the root app widget, `posthog_flutter` still sends events, taps, and screen views (via `PosthogObserver`), but has no visual frames to record—resulting in missing session recordings without throwing errors.\n\n- In [legacy_app.dart](file:///tmp/h-jvd3KC/lib/legacy_app.dart#L13-L23), [`LegacyApp`](file:///tmp/h-jvd3KC/lib/legacy_app.dart#L8-L25) wrapped `MaterialApp` in `PostHogWidget`.\n- In [new_app.dart](file:///tmp/h-jvd3KC/lib/new_app.dart#L19-L36), [`NewApp`](file:///tmp/h-jvd3KC/lib/new_app.dart#L19-L36) returned `MaterialApp.router` directly without wrapping it in `PostHogWidget`.\n\n### Fix\n1. Wrapped `MaterialApp.router` inside `PostHogWidget` in [`NewApp.build`](file:///tmp/h-jvd3KC/lib/new_app.dart#L23-L35) ([new_app.dart](file:///tmp/h-jvd3KC/lib/new_app.dart)).\n2. Documented the root cause and fix in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-jvd3KC/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":53.634322,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":27103,"output_tokens":1960,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":75031,"total_tokens":29063}}}
